{"t": 1794106417.2169032, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_push_files", "args": {"branch": "fix/pagination-57", "files": [{"content": "def page(items: list, number: int, size: int) -> list:\n    \"\"\"Return one page of ``items``; page numbers are 1-based.\"\"\"\n    start = (number - 1) * size\n    return items[start:start + size]\n", "path": "catalog/pager.py"}], "message": "Fix 1-based pagination in page() (#57)", "owner": "acme", "repo": "catalog"}, "ok": true}
{"t": 1794106419.5239663, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_create_pull_request", "args": {"base": "main", "body": "## Problem\n\n`catalog.pager.page()` treated the page number as 0-based, so `page(items, 1, size)` returned the second page. The API documents page numbers as 1-based (`?page=1` is the first page).\n\n## Fix\n\nCompute the offset as `(number - 1) * size`, and document the 1-based contract in a docstring.\n\nFixes #57.\n\n## Verification\n\n```python\nitems = list(range(1, 26))\npage(items, 1, 10)  # [1..10]\npage(items, 2, 10)  # [11..20]\npage(items, 3, 10)  # [21..25]\n```", "head": "fix/pagination-57", "owner": "acme", "repo": "catalog", "title": "Fix 1-based pagination in page() (#57)"}, "ok": true}
